@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
title How a behavioral predicate is concretized: classify at compile time, decide at run time

skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam component {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor #92400E
  FontColor #111827
}

' ── Start: the behavioral guard as written in language! ─────────────────────
rectangle "behavioral guard\n(e.g. safe(P) = ag not bad)" as G #FEF3C7

' ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' COMPILE-TIME LANE — the substrate only CLASSIFIES; it never evaluates the
' algebra on a real process here.
' ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
package "compile time: classify-only" as CT #E0E7FF {
  component "semantic-predicate substrate\nclassify: obligation -> disposition -> quality" as CL #DBEAFE
  rectangle "modal formula => is_satisfiable_3v = DontKnow\nquality = RejectSafeApprox" as CLQ #FEF3C7

  CL --> CLQ
}

note bottom of CT #FEF3C7
  The substrate NEVER evaluates the algebra on a real process at compile time:
  a modal formula is classified semi-decidable (is_satisfiable_3v = DontKnow)
  and tagged RejectSafeApprox. The flip gate admits the rule fail-closed; the
  truth of the guard is deferred to one of the three runtime mechanisms below.
end note

' ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' RUNTIME LANE — the classified guard is DECIDED here by exactly one of three
' concretization mechanisms.
' ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
package "run time: decide the truth" as RT #DCFCE7 {
  component "(i) mu-calculus model check\nHostTerm LTS: successors -> build_lts (cap 10000) -> denote\nEXACT over the reachable LTS" as M1 #FEF3C7
  component "(ii) closed-world facts\nFactBase / runtime snapshot: holds(relation, tuple)\nhalts/safe are host-supplied facts" as M2 #DBEAFE
  component "(iii) host COMM observation\nRhoNativeJoin / Rholang where-boolean / RSpace match\nf1r3node decides at COMM time" as M3 #E0E7FF
}

note right of M1 #FEF3C7
  GAP: only NoTerm and the TestProc fixture implement HostTerm today;
  no real Rholang Par is wired in yet, so modal truth of a dispatched
  process is honestly DontKnow. (ii)/(iii) are how dispatched guards decide.
end note

' ── Flows: guard -> classify -> deferred to one of three runtime mechanisms ──
G --> CL : declared guard
CLQ --> M1 : decide at run time
CLQ --> M2 : decide at run time
CLQ --> M3 : decide at run time

legend right
|= Color / mechanism |= Meaning |
|<#FEF3C7> | semi-decidable leg: DontKnow at compile time; amber gap on (i) |
|<#DBEAFE> | classical / decidable: closed-world facts, holds(relation, tuple) |
|<#E0E7FF> | host / formal: compile-time classify-only lane and (iii) COMM at run time |
|<#DCFCE7> | the runtime decision lane (admitted guard is decided here) |
|= Mechanism |= How the truth is concretely computed |
| (i) mu-calculus | build_lts (cap 10000) -> denote: EXACT over the reachable LTS (HostTerm) |
| (ii) closed-world | FactBase.holds(relation, tuple): halts/safe supplied at run time |
| (iii) host COMM | RhoNativeJoin / where-boolean / RSpace match: f1r3node decides at COMM |
endlegend
@enduml
